if you would like to help the project, you can send an email to cuvensik@gmail.com.

Useless facts
=============
- i came up with this project while reading an article about vim on wikipedia.
- mu, from the word "mouse".
- many programmers write scripts that automatically subscribe to people (most often in python).
- the ss14 creators don't care about newcomers, and they might reject pull requests simply because they don't like your code (they can't even be bothered to write documentation, let alone read the code).
- i drew inspiration from Satoshi Nakamoto and Linus Torvalds.
- corporations parasitize free code (please do not use mit/apache licenses).
- when steve jobs died, the whole world shouted about it; when Dennis Ritchie died, everyone remained silent.
- what do the world's first programmer and the world's first browser (line mode browser) have in common? both were created by women.
- i’d love to work on open-source projects and be independent, but people usually only donate to giants like Linux or Vue.js, not to ordinary programmers :/ (sad...).

